                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_543">Thame, Oxfordshire.
                        Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin. </orgName><p>'This is one of the
                        church bookss of Thame made by me Wylliam Foorest presb' on verso of
                        flyleaf. On Forrest, see ODNB and J. D. Bergsagel in Music and Letters 44
                        (1963) 240--48, for six volumes of music owned by him in 1530. Also owned
                        Cambridge, Trinity College, MSS B. 1. 18 and B. 1. 19; BL MSS Burney 246,
                        285, 295, 341, 344 &amp; 357.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">William Forrest (d. c. 1581).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Robert King (d. 1558), bishop of Oxford,
                     1542. King had been abbot of Thame in Forrest's time.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">After the dissolution it passed from King's
                     hands to Leonard Williams, perhaps his nephew: King's sister had married Sir
                     John Williams of Thame.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given to St John's College by Archbishop
                     William Laud (1573--1645).</provenance>
               </history>
